 ## License
 
 MIT
+
+## CODE compatibility backport
+
+This candidate adds the multi-item/named-export/state-proxy CODE contract from
+upstream `70b23b9fa4dc065c51643988d80c2f45fa8e5901`, with the explicit
+CLICK/TICK or owned-local-page invocation policy from
+`6782e4d5202888ff8ae42d1fc10343ee3cf457ae`.
+`CODE trails` joins the page's Code items, invokes `trails` with the current
+state as `this`, and reports its returned value. Later CODE convenience APIs
+(`this.api.graph`, `body`, `report`, etc.) are outside this narrow backport.
+Existing EXTRACT, EDGES, DEBUG, listener and Solo behavior is retained.
+CODE is a browser-page operation; server-side invocation reports an explicit
+unsupported-context diagnostic before importing source.
